{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_snu633anc35f2pizga5fdesvtciigi2csk3k3uayp23yuncpfptq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01EJj5qbqsuikNn9EjjWhX6c","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-9FeMaj/translated_rust/ERRORS.md","content":"# ERRORS.md — error-surface table (Phase A / Phase C)\n\nDerived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c` by grepping **every** rejection site:\n\n```sh\ngrep -n 'return 0\\|return NULL\\|assert(\\|cp_error_reason =\\|goto cp_err' c_src/src/lib.c\n```\n\nThe C library is compiled **without** `NDEBUG` (the `CMakeLists.txt` sets no\n`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` and no `-DNDEBUG`), so every `assert()` is live and a failure\ncalls `__assert_fail` → `abort()` → the process dies with **SIGABRT**.  The Rust\ntranslation mirrors this with `cp_assert!` → `std::process::abort()` → SIGABRT.\nError-path tests therefore run each call in a *child process* and compare the\nchild's termination status (exit code vs. killed-by-signal-N) in addition to the\nreturned value, the `out` buffer bytes and the `cp_error_reason` string.\n\nLegend for \"expected C result\":\n* `ret 0` – `cp_inflate` returns `0` and `cp_error_reason` points at the quoted\n  string.\n* `SIGABRT` – process aborts inside `assert()`.\n\n| #  | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test | ✔ |\n|----|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|---|\n| 1  | `cp_stored` (lib.c:170) | `LEN != (uint16_t)~NLEN` in a `btype==0` block | `ret 0`, reason `\"Failed to find LEN and NLEN as complements within stored (uncompressed) stream.\"` | `err_len_nlen_mismatch` | [x] |\n| 2  | `cp_stored` (lib.c:179) | `!(s->bits_left / 8 <= (int)LEN)` – stored block is shorter than the remaining input (e.g. trailing bytes after the stored payload) | `ret 0`, reason `\"Stored block extends beyond end of input stream.\"` | `err_stored_beyond_end` | [x] |\n| 3  | `cp_block` (lib.c:254) | literal symbol (`symbol < 256`) decoded but `!(s->out + 1 <= s->out_end)` – `out` buffer full / `out_bytes == 0` | `ret 0`, reason `\"Attempted to overwrite out buffer while outputting a symbol.\"` | `err_out_full_symbol`, `err_out_bytes_zero` | [x] |\n| 4  | `cp_block` (lib.c:273) | back-reference with `!(s->out - backwards_distance >= s->begin)` – distance reaches before the start of `out` | `ret 0`, reason `\"Attempted to write before out buffer (invalid backwards distance).\"` | `err_backdist_before_begin` | [x] |\n| 5  | `cp_block` (lib.c:282) | back-reference with `!(s->out + length <= s->out_end)` – match longer than the room left in `out` | `ret 0`, reason `\"Attempted to overwrite out buffer while outputting a string.\"` | `err_match_past_out_end` | [x] |\n| 6  | `cp_inflate` (lib.c:356) | `btype == 3` (reserved block type) | `ret 0`, reason `\"Detected unknown block type within input stream.\"` | `err_btype3` | [x] |\n| 7  | `cp_unfilter` (lib.c:434) | first row's PNG filter byte `> 4` | `return 0` | *unobservable* – `cp_unfilter` is `static` and **called by nothing** in this translation unit; it is absent from the dynamic symbol table of both `.so`s (asserted by `err_dead_static_not_exported`). Equivalence verified by inspection. | [x] |\n| 8  | `cp_unfilter` (lib.c:468) | a non-first row's PNG filter byte `> 4` | `return 0` | *unobservable*, same as #7 | [x] |\n| 9  | `cp_chunk` (lib.c:397) | `memcmp(start+4, chunk, 4) != 0` **or** `len < minlen` **or** `png->p + len + 12 > png->end` | `return NULL` | *unobservable*, same as #7 (`cp_chunk` is `static`, uncalled) | [x] |\n| 10 | `cp_find` (lib.c:409) | no chunk with the requested id / `minlen` found before `png->end` (loop falls through) | `return NULL` | *unobservable*, same as #7 (`cp_find` is `static`, uncalled) | [x] |\n| 11 | `cp_ptr` (lib.c:89) | `s->bits_left & 7` – a `btype==0` block reached while the bit cursor is not byte-aligned w.r.t. `bits_left`; happens after the *partial* final word was folded in at a `count % 8 != 0` boundary | `SIGABRT` | `abort_cp_ptr_misaligned` | [x] |\n| 12 | `cp_peak_bits` (lib.c:98) | `s->word_index > s->word_count` after the post-increment | `SIGABRT` | *unreachable by construction*: the increment is guarded by `if (s->word_index < s->word_count)`, so the post-increment value is `<= word_count`. Present and identical in Rust (`cp_assert!((*s).word_index <= (*s).word_count)`); asserted unreachable by `unreach_word_index` (fuzz never trips it in either lib). | [x] |\n| 13 | `cp_consume_bits` (lib.c:109) | `s->count < num_bits_to_read` – truncated stream where `bits_left + count >= n` (so the overflow assert passes) but only `count < n` bits are actually buffered | `SIGABRT` | `abort_consume_underflow` | [x] |\n| 14 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:117) | `num_bits_to_read > 32` – reachable through the **writable exported table** `cp_len_extra_bits` / `cp_dist_extra_bits` (`uint8_t`, so up to 255) | `SIGABRT` | `abort_read_bits_gt32_len`, `abort_read_bits_gt32_dist` | [x] |\n| 15 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:118) | `num_bits_to_read < 0` | `SIGABRT` | *unreachable by construction*: every call site passes a literal (`1,2,3,4,5,7,16`), `s->count & 7` (`0..7`, and `count >= 0` is enforced by assert #13), or a `uint8_t` table element (`0..255`). Present and identical in Rust. | [x] |\n| 16 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:119) | `s->bits_left <= 0` – `in_bytes == 0`, `in_bytes < 0`, or the stream ran dry | `SIGABRT` | `abort_in_bytes_zero`, `abort_in_bytes_negative`, `abort_stream_exhausted` | [x] |\n| 17 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:120) | `s->count > 64` | `SIGABRT` | *unreachable by construction*: `count` grows only in `cp_peak_bits`, guarded by `count < num_bits_to_read`; `num_bits_to_read <= 32` is asserted (#14) before every `cp_peak_bits` from `cp_read_bits`, and `cp_decode` peaks with a literal 16, so `count <= 15 + 32 = 47` at most. Present and identical in Rust. | [x] |\n| 18 | `cp_read_bits` (lib.c:121) | `cp_would_overflow(s, n)`, i.e. `(bits_left + count) - n < 0` – stream truncated | `SIGABRT` | `abort_would_overflow` | [x] |\n| 19 | `cp_build` (lib.c:148) | a code length `>= 16`; reachable through the writable exported `cp_fixed_table` | `SIGABRT` | `abort_build_len_ge16` | [x] |\n| 20 | `cp_decode` (lib.c:211) | `(search >> len) != (key >> len)` – the buffered bits do not match any code of the (incomplete / over-subscribed) Huffman tree | `SIGABRT` | `abort_decode_no_match` | [x] |\n\n## Generic FFI boundary conditions (also covered, though not distinct C rows)\n\n| # | case | notes | test | ✔ |\n|---|------|-------|------|---|\n| G1 | `cp_inflate(NULL, 0, NULL, 0)` | `in_bytes*8 == 0` → assert #16 fires before any dereference; NULL is never read | `abort_null_in_zero_len` | [x] |\n| G2 | `cp_inflate(in, 0, out, n)` | `bits_left == 0` → assert #16 | `abort_in_bytes_zero` | [x] |\n| G3 | `cp_inflate(in, n, out, 0)` | `out_end == out`; first literal → error #3 | `err_out_bytes_zero` | [x] |\n| G4 | `cp_inflate(in, n, out, negative)` | `out_end < out` → error #3 on the first literal | `err_out_bytes_negative` | [x] |\n| G5 | `cp_inflate(in, negative, …)` | `bits_left = in_bytes*8 < 0` → assert #16 | `abort_in_bytes_negative` | [x] |\n| G6 | `cp_inflate` with `in_bytes` huge (`INT_MAX`, `0x20000000` → `in_bytes*8` overflows to 0) | signed overflow wraps identically (`wrapping_mul`), then assert #16 | `abort_in_bytes_overflow` | [x] |\n| G7 | `convert_pix` with `bpp` outside the `switch` (`0`, `5`, `255`, `-1`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`) — a C `switch` on an `int` accepts **any** value, i.e. \"out-of-range enum\" across FFI | no store to `dst`, but `src += bpp` still runs `w*h` times, and `src++` runs `h` times | `cfg_convert_pix_bpp_out_of_range` | [x] |\n| G8 | `convert_pix` with `w <= 0` and/or `h <= 0` (incl. `INT_MIN`) | loops do not execute, `dst` untouched | `cfg_convert_pix_degenerate` | [x] |\n| G9 | `convert_pix(bpp, 0, 0, NULL, NULL)` | `h <= 0` → no dereference of the NULL pointers | `cfg_convert_pix_degenerate` | [x] |\n| G10 | `btype` value space | `btype` is 2 bits, so `0,1,2,3` is the complete set; `3` is row #6, `0/1/2` are valid | `err_btype3` + Phase B rows | [x] |\n| G11 | reserved length symbols 286/287 and distance symbols 30/31 (one step past the documented ranges 257..285 / 0..29) | `cp_len_base[29]=cp_len_base[30]=0`, `cp_dist_base[30]=cp_dist_base[31]=0` → `length`/`distance` become the extra bits only (`0`), so `distance == 0` → row #4 fires (`out - 0 >= begin` is *true*, so it does **not** fire; instead a zero-length match with `src == dst` is copied) | `cfg_reserved_len_dist_symbols` | [x] |\n| G12 | exported tables mutated to values that stay in range | library must read the tables **live** from the exported symbols | `cfg_table_mutation_*` | [x] |\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14525,"cache_read_input_tokens":79387,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14525,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a438d629-c807-4b9d-ac71-026d3fe26fa4","uuid":"53f28228-c89b-4c8b-9e48-77533ca1104d","timestamp":"2026-08-20T18:13:53.907Z"}
