{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4bgr5cjp63irbfis2qteocng75lwqhni3twgsfxit2q3nkuyk54q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What was done\n\n**Phase A — artifacts** (`SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, all derived mechanically from the C source):\n- Build surface: `Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]`** (`cargo metadata` → `\"features\": {}`) and `c_src` has **no `#if/#ifdef/#define`** and no CMake `option()` → exactly one feature combination. Verified under dev, `--no-default-features`, and `--release`.\n- `SYMBOLS.md`: all **9** C dynamic symbols, same `nm` class and byte-identical data sizes. **Symbol diff is empty**; 19 `static` C functions are correctly absent from *both* `.so`s.\n- `ERRORS.md`: 20 rejection rows + 14 generic FFI boundary rows.\n- `CONFIGS.md`: 40 valid-configuration rows over the axes the C actually branches on.\n\n**Harness** (`tests/diff.rs`, `harness = false`): loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading` — never calls Rust directly — and `fork()`s per case so aborts, segfaults and *non-termination* are comparable. Per case it compares the return value, every byte of the out arena (including the C's unchecked overrun), the `cp_error_reason` string, a hash of the in arena, and the exact termination status. Assertion rows also grep the C's stderr to prove the *intended* `assert()` fired.\n\n**Result: 84 groups / 8015 cases / 626 identical non-zero terminations / 0 failures** in all three configurations.\n\n## Real divergences found and fixed in the Rust\n\n1. **Integer-overflow traps.** `in_bytes * 8`, `in_bytes - first_bytes` etc. wrap in C but *trapped* in Rust's debug profile. All arithmetic converted to `wrapping_*`. Caught by `abort_in_bytes_min_align{0..3}` (C segfaults, Rust used to abort with a panic).\n2. **`cp_dynamic` stack-frame corruption.** A code-18 run adds up to 138 entries against a bound of 320, so the C writes over its own locals. `fuzz38` case 100 diverged as *C = timeout / Rust = SIGABRT*. The Rust now models the C frame byte-for-byte (offsets read from `objdump -d`), reproducing all three regimes — including inputs where writing `lens[376]` clears the low byte of `n`, snapping it back to 256 so **the C never terminates** and the Rust now doesn't either (`ovs_c_nonterminating`, `ovs_d_transition_band`, 12 `fuzz38` cases).\n3. **`lenlens` index panic** when `cp_permutation_order` holds a value > 18.\n\nTwo things are documented as *not* reproducible rather than papered over: `cp_permutation_order` values ≥ 28 (C corrupts the *caller's* frame), and the purely temporal fact that `-O0` C really runs `h` empty iterations for `convert_pix(bpp, w<=0, h)` while optimised Rust deletes the dead loop.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":948,"cache_read_input_tokens":335968,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":948,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a438d629-c807-4b9d-ac71-026d3fe26fa4","uuid":"7fa9f499-61e7-41f1-9400-fbb411919a47","timestamp":"2026-08-20T20:19:29.414Z"}
